post.description:
Queues up to **100 products** (each with **1–50 variants**) for async creation via BullMQ. Returns a `batchId` that the frontend polls for progress via `GET /api/v1/products/bulk/{batchId}`.

Requires `products:bulk:write` permission.
Rate limit: **5 per hour per staff member** (shared with POST /bulk/excel).

---

## Two-step image flow (REQUIRED if you want images)

Because this endpoint accepts JSON — not multipart — images must be uploaded separately **before** calling this endpoint. The workflow is:

```
Step 1 ─ POST /api/v1/products/images/bulk-upload
          multipart/form-data
          Field: images[]  (up to 50 files)
          Field: keys      JSON array of unique string keys, one per file

          Response:
          {
            "images": {
              "brake-pad-hero":   { "url": "...", "storagePublicId": "...", "storageProvider": "cloudinary", "width": 1200, "height": 900, "bytes": 78432 },
              "brake-pad-detail": { "url": "...", "storagePublicId": "...", "storageProvider": "cloudinary", "width": 1200, "height": 900, "bytes": 64100 },
              "oil-filter-main":  { "url": "...", "storagePublicId": "...", "storageProvider": "cloudinary", "width": 1200, "height": 900, "bytes": 55000 }
            }
          }

Step 2 ─ POST /api/v1/products/bulk
          application/json
          Pass the entire "images" object you received in step 1 as the
          "uploadedImages" field in the body. Then reference individual images
          inside your products using the same keys.
```

If you have **no images**, pass an empty object: `"uploadedImages": {}`.

---

## Request body — full field reference

### Top-level fields

| Field | Type | Required | Constraints |
|---|---|---|---|
| `idempotencyKey` | string | **Yes** | 8–100 chars. See idempotency section. |
| `uploadedImages` | object | **Yes** | Key → image metadata map from Step 1. Pass `{}` if no images. |
| `products` | array | **Yes** | 1–100 items |

### `uploadedImages` object shape

Returned verbatim from `POST /images/bulk-upload`. Pass it through as-is.

```typescript
uploadedImages: {
  [key: string]: {
    url: string;                          // Cloudinary/S3 CDN URL
    storagePublicId: string;              // Cloudinary public_id or S3 object key
    storageProvider: "cloudinary" | "s3"; // Storage backend used
    width?: number;                       // Pixels (optional)
    height?: number;                      // Pixels (optional)
    bytes?: number;                       // File size in bytes (optional)
  }
}
```

---

### Product fields

Each item in the `products` array:

| Field | Type | Required | Constraints | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `categoryId` | uuid | **Yes** | DB UUID format | Use the `id` field from GET /categories — NOT `CAT-XXXXXXXX` |
| `brandId` | uuid | **Yes** | DB UUID format | Use the `id` field from GET /brands — NOT `BRD-XXXXXXXX` |
| `name` | string | **Yes** | 3–255 chars, trimmed | Must be unique within the batch |
| `description` | string | **Yes** | 10–10,000 chars, trimmed | |
| `slug` | string | No | 2–280 chars, lowercase/numbers/hyphens only | Auto-generated from `name` if omitted |
| `isActive` | boolean | No | — | Default: `true` |
| `isFeatured` | boolean | No | — | Default: `false` |
| `variants` | array | **Yes** | 1–50 items | At least one required per product |
| `specifications` | array | No | — | Default: `[]` |
| `images` | object | No | Key → image reference map | Keys must exist in `uploadedImages` |

### Product `images` field

Associates pre-uploaded images with a specific product. Keys must match keys from the top-level `uploadedImages` map.

```typescript
images: {
  [key: string]: {
    key: string;          // Same key — must exist in uploadedImages
    altText?: string;     // Alt text for accessibility (max 255 chars)
    isPrimary?: boolean;  // Default: false. Only one image should be primary.
    sortOrder?: number;   // Integer ≥ 0. Lower = displayed first.
  }
}
```

Example — product with two images, first one set as primary:
```json
"images": {
  "brake-pad-hero":   { "key": "brake-pad-hero",   "isPrimary": true,  "sortOrder": 0, "altText": "Brake pad front view" },
  "brake-pad-detail": { "key": "brake-pad-detail",  "isPrimary": false, "sortOrder": 1, "altText": "Brake pad detail" }
}
```

---

### Variant fields

Each item in the `variants` array:

| Field | Type | Required | Constraints | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `name` | string | **Yes** | 1–255 chars | e.g. "Standard", "UK 9 / Black" |
| `price` | number | **Yes** | positive, max 2 decimals | Selling price. A markup rule may be applied on top if one exists for this category+brand. |
| `costPrice` | number | **Yes** | positive, max 2 decimals, must be ≤ price | Internal cost |
| `sku` | string | No | max 100 chars | Auto-generated if omitted |
| `condition` | enum | No | `NEW` | `USED` | `REFURBISHED` | `OPEN_BOX` | Default: `NEW` |
| `sourcingType` | enum | No | `INHOUSE` | `OUTSOURCED` | Default: `INHOUSE` |
| `compareAtPrice` | number | null | No | positive, must be **greater than** price | Crossed-out original price |
| `stockQuantity` | integer | No | ≥ 0 | Default: `0` |
| `lowStockThreshold` | integer | No | ≥ 0 | Default: `10` |
| `weight` | number | No | positive | For shipping calculations |
| `imageUrl` | string | No | valid URL | Variant image — direct URL path. Use this when the URL is already known (e.g. an external CDN link). Cannot be used together with `imageKey` on the same variant. |
| `imageKey` | string | No | max 100 chars, must exist in `uploadedImages` | Variant image — key reference path. Use this during bulk creation when the image was pre-uploaded via `POST /images/bulk-upload`. The worker resolves the key to its CDN URL before saving. Cannot be used together with `imageUrl` on the same variant. |
| `isActive` | boolean | No | — | Default: `true` |
| `attributes` | array | No | name 1–50 chars, value 1–100 chars | e.g. `[{ "name": "Color", "value": "Black" }]` |

**Cross-field variant rules (batch rejected on failure):**
- `compareAtPrice > price` when provided
- `costPrice ≤ price` always

---

### Variant images — detailed explanation

Each variant supports **one image** stored as a single URL on the `ProductVariant` record (`imageUrl` column). This is distinct from the product-level image gallery (the `ProductImage` table, which supports multiple images with sort order, alt text, and a primary flag).

**When to use a variant image:**
Use it to show the specific visual for that variant — typically a colour swatch, size-specific thumbnail, or condition-specific photo (e.g. a "Used" variant showing actual wear). The product gallery handles the main product photography; the variant image is the per-option swatch shown in size/colour selectors.

**Two ways to set a variant image in bulk creation:**

#### Path A — `imageKey` (recommended for bulk upload)

Pre-upload the image via `POST /images/bulk-upload` in Step 1, then reference it by key in the variant:

```json
// Step 1 — upload all images including variant swatches
// Keys uploaded: ["brake-pad-hero", "brake-pad-standard-swatch", "brake-pad-premium-swatch"]

// Step 2 — POST /bulk body
{
  "uploadedImages": {
    "brake-pad-hero":            { "url": "https://...", "storagePublicId": "...", "storageProvider": "cloudinary" },
    "brake-pad-standard-swatch": { "url": "https://...", "storagePublicId": "...", "storageProvider": "cloudinary" },
    "brake-pad-premium-swatch":  { "url": "https://...", "storagePublicId": "...", "storageProvider": "cloudinary" }
  },
  "products": [{
    "name": "Brake Pad Set - Front",
    "description": "...",
    "images": {
      "brake-pad-hero": { "key": "brake-pad-hero", "isPrimary": true, "sortOrder": 0 }
    },
    "variants": [
      {
        "name": "Standard",
        "price": 89.99,
        "costPrice": 45.00,
        "imageKey": "brake-pad-standard-swatch"
      },
      {
        "name": "Premium",
        "price": 129.99,
        "costPrice": 70.00,
        "imageKey": "brake-pad-premium-swatch"
      }
    ]
  }]
}
```

The same key can be used in both a product's `images` block **and** a variant's `imageKey` field simultaneously — for example if the hero shot is also the swatch for the default variant.

#### Path B — `imageUrl` (for externally hosted images)

If the image is already hosted on an external CDN or you are building a non-bulk single-product flow, pass the full URL directly:

```json
"variants": [
  {
    "name": "Black",
    "price": 89.99,
    "costPrice": 45.00,
    "imageUrl": "https://your-cdn.com/products/brake-pad-black-swatch.jpg"
  }
]
```

> **Do not use both `imageKey` and `imageUrl` on the same variant.** If both are present, `imageKey` takes precedence and `imageUrl` is ignored by the worker.

#### No variant image

Simply omit both fields. The variant will have `imageUrl: null` in the database and the storefront falls back to the product's primary image for display.

```json
"variants": [
  { "name": "Standard", "price": 89.99, "costPrice": 45.00 }
]
```

---

### Specification fields

| Field | Type | Required | Constraints |
|---|---|---|---|
| `name` | string | **Yes** | 1–100 chars |
| `value` | string | **Yes** | 1–255 chars |
| `sortOrder` | integer | No | ≥ 0, default `0` |

---

## Markup rules interaction

If a markup rule exists for a product's `categoryId` + `brandId` combination, the prices you supply in `price` and `compareAtPrice` are **automatically adjusted** before being saved. The markup is applied server-side — you do not need to do anything extra. If you want to preview what the final prices will be before submission, use `POST /pricing/markup-rules/preview` first.

---

