## How the returned data maps into POST /bulk

```typescript
const uploadedImages = await bulkUploadImages([
  { file: heroFile,   key: 'brake-pad-hero' },
  { file: detailFile, key: 'brake-pad-detail' },
]);

// uploadedImages is now:
// {
//   "brake-pad-hero":   { url: "...", storagePublicId: "...", storageProvider: "cloudinary", ... },
//   "brake-pad-detail": { url: "...", storagePublicId: "...", storageProvider: "cloudinary", ... }
// }

await fetch('/api/v1/products/bulk', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    idempotencyKey: sessionStorage.getItem('bulkProductUploadKey'),
    uploadedImages, // ← pass the whole object through unchanged
    products: [
      {
        categoryId: '11111111-...',
        brandId: '22222222-...',
        name: 'Brake Pad Set - Front',
        description: 'Ceramic front brake pads...',
        images: {
          // Reference keys from uploadedImages — only assign the images that belong to THIS product
          'brake-pad-hero':   { key: 'brake-pad-hero',   isPrimary: true,  sortOrder: 0, altText: 'Brake pad front view' },
          'brake-pad-detail': { key: 'brake-pad-detail',  isPrimary: false, sortOrder: 1 },
        },
        variants: [
          { name: 'Standard', price: 89.99, costPrice: 45.00, stockQuantity: 50 }
        ]
      }
    ]
  })
});
```

---

## Important notes

**Image ownership:** There is no server-side validation that a key used in one product's `images` block isn't also used in another product's `images` block. The key→URL map is shared across the whole batch. If you share an image between two products, both will reference the same Cloudinary/S3 URL — this is intentional and supported.

**Orphaned images:** If an image key is included in `uploadedImages` but never referenced in any product's `images` block, it will be uploaded to storage but never persisted in the database. This wastes storage. Only upload images you actually intend to use.

**Re-uploading on retry:** The `POST /images/bulk-upload` endpoint is NOT idempotent. Each call uploads fresh files to storage and returns new URLs. If Step 1 succeeds but Step 2 fails, you should **reuse the `uploadedImages` response from Step 1** rather than re-uploading. Cache it in component state for the duration of the retry loop:

```typescript
let cachedUploadedImages: Record<string, UploadedImageMeta> | null = null;

async function submitWithRetry(products, imageFiles) {
  // Only upload images once — reuse the result on retries
  if (!cachedUploadedImages) {
    cachedUploadedImages = await bulkUploadImages(imageFiles);
  }

  return fetch('/api/v1/products/bulk', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify({
      idempotencyKey: sessionStorage.getItem('bulkProductUploadKey'),
      uploadedImages: cachedUploadedImages,
      products,
    }),
  });
}
```

**Rate limit header:** A successful response includes `X-RateLimit-Remaining` showing how many bulk image uploads remain in the current hour window.

get.description:
Call this immediately after the customer is redirected back from the hosted checkout page (Miden or Paystack).

---

## When to call this

When Miden/Paystack redirect the customer back to your `callbackUrl`, they append the reference as a query param:

```
https://yoursite.com/payment/callback?reference=MDN-1A2B3C4D-E5F6A7B8
                                       ↑ extract this
```

Read `reference` from the URL and call this endpoint.

---

## Frontend callback page example

```ts
// On your /payment/callback page:
const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
const reference = params.get('reference')
    ?? sessionStorage.getItem('pendingPaymentRef');

const res = await fetch(`/api/v1/payments/verify/${reference}`, {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },
});
const { data } = await res.json();

if (data.status === 'PAID') {
  // Clear cart, show success screen
  clearCart();
  router.push(`/orders/${data.orderId}/success`);

} else if (data.status === 'FAILED') {
  // Show error, offer retry
  router.push('/checkout?error=payment_failed');

} else if (data.status === 'PENDING') {
  // Payment is still being processed
  // Poll GET /api/v1/payments/{paymentId} every few seconds
  const paymentId = sessionStorage.getItem('pendingPaymentId');
  startPolling(paymentId);
}
```

---

## Response status meanings

| status | Meaning | What to show |
|---|---|---|
| `PAID` | Payment confirmed ✅ | Success screen, clear cart, show order |
| `FAILED` | Payment declined ❌ | Error message, "try again" button |
| `PENDING` | Not yet confirmed ⏳ | "Processing…" spinner, poll `GET /payments/{paymentId}` |

---

## What "verify" actually does (Miden)

The hosted checkout page lets the customer pay by **card or bank transfer** — the frontend never chooses which, and the response doesn't tell you in advance which one they'll use. Because of that, this endpoint checks **both channels** on every call: it looks for a matching Cards transaction first, and if that comes up empty, it checks Virtual Account (bank transfer) transactions before giving up. You don't need to know or send which channel the customer picked — this happens automatically.

A `PENDING` response means neither channel has a settled record yet — this is normal immediately after redirect, especially for bank transfers (the customer may still be completing the transfer in their banking app). Keep polling `GET /payments/{paymentId}`; there is no separate "which channel" step for the frontend to handle.

---

## Rate limit
20 verify calls per customer per 5 minutes.

Returns full payment details for a payment the customer owns.

---

## When to use this

Use this to **poll for status** when `GET /verify` returns `PENDING`.
Webhooks update the payment in the background — this endpoint reflects the latest state.

```ts
async function pollPaymentStatus(paymentId: string) {
  const MAX_ATTEMPTS = 12;   // 12 × 5s = 60 seconds max
  const INTERVAL_MS  = 5000;

  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < MAX_ATTEMPTS; attempt++) {
    await sleep(INTERVAL_MS);

    const res = await fetch(`/api/v1/payments/${paymentId}`, {
      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },
    });
    const { data } = await res.json();

    if (data.status === 'PAID') {
      showSuccess(data.orderId);
      return;
    }
    if (data.status === 'FAILED') {
      showError(data.errorMessage);
      return;
    }
    // else still PENDING — keep polling
  }

  // Timeout — tell customer to check their email / contact support
  showTimeout();
}
```

---

## paymentId format

The `paymentId` is the `PMT-XXXX` value from the initiate response — **not** a UUID.

```
GET /api/v1/payments/PMT-A1B2C3D4E5F6A7B8C9D0
```

---

## Response includes refund history

If staff have recorded any refunds on this payment, they appear in the `refunds` array.

## Socket Authentication

The chat real-time layer uses Socket.IO over WebSocket, connecting to the `/ws` namespace.

The token is **not** passed as an HTTP `Authorization` header. It must be passed in the Socket.IO `auth` object:

```js
import { io } from 'socket.io-client';

const socket = io('https://your-api.com/ws', {
  auth: {
    token: 'your_jwt_here'   // ← server reads socket.handshake.auth.token
  },
  transports: ['websocket'],
});
```

### Fallback priority (if auth object not used)
1. `socket.handshake.auth.token` ← **preferred**
2. `socket.handshake.query.token` (appears in URL / server logs — avoid)
3. `Cookie: staffAccessToken` or `Cookie: accessToken` (automatic if using httpOnly cookies)

### Connection errors
Listen for `connect_error` to handle auth failures:

```js
socket.on('connect_error', (err) => {
  // err.message will be one of:
  // "Unauthorized — no token provided"
  // "Session expired — please log in again"
  // "Unauthorized — invalid token"
  // "Account not found"
  // "Account deactivated"
});
```

### On connect — Staff
- Automatically joins `staff:room` broadcast room
- Receives `presence:list` (snapshot of who's online)
- Receives `staffroom:history` (recent staff room messages)
- All other staff receive `presence:staff:online`
- Server drains waiting queue and assigns any pending conversations

### On connect — Customer
- If an active conversation exists, socket is automatically joined to `conv:{conversationId}` room
- Receives `chat:conversation:updated` with current status

### Heartbeat (Staff only)
Staff must emit `presence:heartbeat` every **30 seconds** to stay marked as online:

```js
socket.emit('presence:heartbeat');
const hb = setInterval(() => socket.emit('presence:heartbeat'), 30_000);
socket.on('disconnect', () => clearInterval(hb));
```

Opens a persistent Server-Sent Events connection. The server pushes a `log` event after every request finishes processing.

**On connect**, the last 20 entries are sent as a catch-up burst so the dashboard is immediately populated.

**Heartbeat**: a blank SSE comment (`: heartbeat`) is sent every 30 seconds to prevent Koyeb / nginx from closing idle connections. The browser `EventSource` API ignores comment lines automatically.

**Authentication note**: The browser `EventSource` API does not support custom headers. Use a cookie-based auth session or a fetch-based SSE client library that supports headers.

**Event types:**
| Event | When | Payload |
|---|---|---|
| `connected` | On connect | `{ ts: ISO date }` |
| `log` | After every request finishes | Same shape as list-view item (no stack trace, no requestBody). Always fired — even for requests not persisted due to sampling. |
| `anomaly` | When anomaly detector fires (every 60 s check) | `{ timestamp, type, windowMins, current, baseline, factor, routeSamples }` — same shape as `GET /api/v1/monitor/anomalies` items |

**Example (browser):**
```js
const es = new EventSource('/api/v1/monitor/live');
es.addEventListener('connected', e => console.log('connected at', JSON.parse(e.data).ts));
es.addEventListener('log', e => {
  const entry = JSON.parse(e.data);
  console.log(entry.method, entry.path, entry.statusCode, entry.duration + 'ms');
});
es.addEventListener('anomaly', e => {
  const a = JSON.parse(e.data);
  console.warn('Anomaly:', a.type, '— factor', a.factor, 'x baseline');
});
```

Requires SUPER_ADMIN role.

